From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Dylan Ironside <dylan@dylanironside.io>
Date: Thu, 5 Nov 2026 04:29:58 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: apple: t8132-j604: Enable the G16 GPU

Enable the ASC mailbox and the GFX TVM gate, keep the GPU enabled, and
make the TVM gate the parent of the GFX PMGR domain, as the J713 GPU
description in Aurora does (t8132-j713-gpu.dtsi). The node addresses,
interrupts and the TVM gate register were checked against the J604 ADT
when the J604 GPU description was added; only the status lines and the
ps_gfx parent change. This replaces the identity-report-only enable of
the gpu node with the J713 form.

The G16 backend needs both: the firmware is driven over agx_mbox
(mboxes = <&agx_mbox>), and the GFX domain it holds during admission is
the one the J713 powers through the outer TVM gate.

m1n1 still fills the six firmware and UAT reservations and the firmware
segment layout at boot, and leaves the gpu status alone. asahi has no
module alias for apple,agx-t8132, so nothing probes the GPU until
userspace loads the module, and the G16 backend admits the J604 only on
a firmware build measured on a J604.

Signed-off-by: Dylan Ironside <dylan@dylanironside.io>
Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5.5
(rebased from commit 9546b5ac371a28136b8892ff7d3fa6ca21a0e2da onto the gpu-okay commit 22fab5f8f5)
---
 arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/t8132-j604-gpu.dtsi | 26 ++++++++-----------
 1 file changed, 11 insertions(+), 15 deletions(-)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/t8132-j604-gpu.dtsi b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/t8132-j604-gpu.dtsi
index b6d97e04fa..a53e6b2791 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/t8132-j604-gpu.dtsi
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/t8132-j604-gpu.dtsi
@@ -9,10 +9,11 @@
  * publishes the firmware segment layout on the gpu node; it never enables
  * the gpu node itself.
  *
- * The mailbox and the GFX TVM gate stay disabled: the G16 backend is
- * qualified on J713 only, and the J604 perf-state selection and loaded
- * firmware image are not measured yet. ps_gfx keeps its current parent.
- * The gpu node itself is enabled only for the identity report below.
+ * The GPU, its mailbox and the GFX TVM gate are enabled in the J713 form:
+ * the outer TVM gate is the parent of the GFX PMGR domain. The G16 backend
+ * admits the J604 only on a firmware build measured on a J604, and asahi
+ * has no module alias for this node, so nothing probes it until userspace
+ * loads the module.
  *
  * DTV-<id> tags name rows of DT-VERIFY-gpu.tsv.
  *
@@ -68,7 +69,6 @@
 		compatible = "apple,t8132-gfx-tvm";
 		reg = <0x3 0x80760800 0x0 0x4>; /* DTV-GPU-11 */
 		#power-domain-cells = <0>;
-		status = "disabled"; /* DTV-GPU-13 */
 	};
 
 	gpu: gpu@302600000 {
@@ -85,15 +85,6 @@
 				<&gpu_shared_l2>, <&gpu_fw_text>, <&gpu_fw_data>;
 		memory-region-names = "ttbs", "pagetables", "handoff",
 				      "shared-l2", "fw-text", "fw-data";
-		/*
-		 * Enabled for the G16 identity report only: the backend refuses
-		 * the J604 before the PMP, its own power-domain hold or the
-		 * firmware (the driver core still powers ps_gfx for the probe
-		 * and off again when it fails), and m1n1 disables this node
-		 * again if the handoff does not match. The mailbox, gfx_tvm and
-		 * the reservations stay as they are.
-		 */
-		status = "okay"; /* DTV-GPU-7 */
 	};
 
 	agx_mbox: mailbox@302608000 {
@@ -108,6 +99,11 @@
 		interrupt-names = "send-empty", "send-not-empty",
 				  "recv-empty", "recv-not-empty";
 		#mbox-cells = <0>;
-		status = "disabled"; /* DTV-GPU-10 */
 	};
 };
+
+/* The outer TVM gate is the parent of the GFX PMGR domain, as on J713. */
+&ps_gfx {
+	status = "okay";
+	power-domains = <&gfx_tvm>;
+};
